.TH REDLINE 1 "2025" "redline 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redline \- a read-focused TUI code browser for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redline
[options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Redline is an emacs/helm/magit-flavored code browser that lives in a terminal
pane. It provides instant navigation (files, symbols, definitions, references,
grep), a git status/staging/commit surface, live file watching, and light
editing (commit messages, per-project notes).
.PP
Redline can also be driven from outside: with no subcommand it is the TUI;
with a subcommand (or repeatable \fB-c\fR command lines) it becomes a control
client. When a control socket is reachable the verbs drive the LIVE session
(the human's screen moves); otherwise they run an ephemeral headless session.
See \fIdocs/control-api.md\fR for the JSON snapshot schema and the full verb
table.
.SH CONTROL VERBS
.TP
\fBredline state [--json]\fR
Print the observable session state (text, or JSON with \fB--json\fR).
.TP
\fBredline quote\fR
Print the current frame as text (an 80-column approximation. see docs/control-api.md).
.TP
\fBredline buffer [START..END]\fR
Print the current buffer's text (optionally a 1-based inclusive line range).
.TP
\fBredline notes [--plain]\fR
Print the annotation dump.
.TP
\fBredline do NAME [ARG]\fR Dispatch a registry command.
.TP
\fBredline key TOKEN\fR \fBredline keys SEQ\fR \fBredline text LITERAL\fR
Feed one key, a key sequence, or literal text through the same routing the
terminal uses.
.TP
\fBredline open PATH[:LINE[:COL]]\fR
Open a project-relative file and land the point (1-based line/column).
.TP
\fBredline goto LINE\fR Land the point on LINE (1-based).
.TP
\fBredline jump SYMBOL\fR Open the symbol picker filtered to SYMBOL.
.TP
\fBredline search QUERY\fR \fBredline isearch QUERY\fR
Start a project search / an in-buffer incremental search.
.TP
\fBredline select [N|next|prev]\fR \fBredline confirm\fR
Move the picker selection / accept it.
.TP
\fBredline cancel\fR The global cancel (C-g equivalent).
.TP
\fBredline annotate TEXT\fR Annotate at point.
.TP
\fBredline magit\fR Open magit status.
.TP
\fBredline quit\fR Ask the session to exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
See the README.md for the full keymap cheat sheet. Common bindings:
.TP
\fBC-x C-f\fR Find a file in the project
.TP
\fBC-x g\fR Magit status (stage, unstage, commit)
.TP
\fBM-\fR.\fR Jump to the definition under point
.TP
\fBC-s\fR Incremental search forward
.TP
\fBM-x\fR Command palette
.TP
\fBC-x C-c\fR Quit
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket PATH\fR
The control socket to bind (TUI) or connect to (client). Defaults to
\fB$REDLINE_SOCKET\fR, else \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/redline-<uid>.sock\fR, else
\fB/tmp/redline-<uid>.sock\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-attached\fR
Require a reachable control socket: a missing socket is a hard error (exit 1)
even for an env-only socket, instead of falling back to a headless session.
.TP
\fB\-\-project DIR\fR The project root a headless session opens (default `.`).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR Emit \fBstate\fR as JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-width N\fR / \fB\-\-height N\fR The headless session / render geometry.
.TP
\fB\-c CMD\fR Repeatable: run a command line (verb + optional argument) in order.
.TP
\fB\-\-notes=plain\fR
On quit, print the annotation dump in the bare grep-addressable form
`path:line: text` (no header, no code lines, no orphan marker). The
default block form carries the orphan marker; see README.md.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.I REDLINE_SOCKET
The control socket path when \fB\-\-socket\fR is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/redline/config.toml
Configuration: theme, auto_reload, key-binding overrides.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/redline/
Project registry, recents, and highlight cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit\fR(1), \fBemacs\fR(1)
.SH AUTHOR
Redline contributors.
